            <ArticleTitle>Shaping Science for Increasing Interdependence and Specialization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-124</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0166-2236(16)30192-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tins.2016.12.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Like art, science affords an individualistic career. However, increasingly, complexity necessitates increased interdependency and specialization. Despite this change, many institutions, funding agencies, and publishers insist on an exclusively individualistic model of science. This hinders scientific progress by imposing a range of inefficiencies in the planning and execution of research plans.</AbstractText>
